id: pm-hrhfgi
title: "GH-1214: Bound complete item reads and isolate Git newline fixtures on Windows"
description: Nightly Windows Node 24 run 34104192850 exposes unreadable items in the 10000-item aggregate fixture and a CRLF byte mismatch after rebase abort. Preserve complete reads with bounded filesystem concurrency and deterministic repository newline policy.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-07T13:34:48.714Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-07T13:58:45.530Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-07T13:55:19.153Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-07T13:55:19.153Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Complete 10000-item aggregation passes on Windows without shrinking the fixture; bounded descriptor-pressure reads return every readable item; permission failures remain visible; aborted rebase preserves exact fixture bytes and rejects stale Git proof.
goal: project management = context management
value: Reliable complete-corpus SDK queries and portable recovery assurance
why_now: New GitHub report exposes an uncovered boundary in required release or agent workflows.
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: Bound authoritative item scans in batches of 32 and explicitly isolate exact-byte rebase fixtures from host newline policy.
expected_result: Large complete-corpus reads do not manufacture unreadable files through descriptor exhaustion; genuine unreadable sources remain visible and Git restoration proofs retain exact byte checks.
actual_result: Descriptor-pressure negative control failed before the fix and now retains all 128 readable items while reporting a real denied item. All linked tests including the 10000-item aggregate and rebase-abort proof pass. Full exact coverage and static gates pass; hosted Windows verification remains required before merge.
